WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:07.731
A proof is a chain of allowed steps, from what you know to what you claim. Here is the claim: if p and q, then q and p.

00:08.131 --> 00:14.426
First, assume h: p and q. This introduces the hypothesis, leaving q and p to prove.

00:14.826 --> 00:20.228
Next, take h apart by cases. Now hp proves p, and hq proves q.

00:20.628 --> 00:27.246
To build q and p, it suffices to prove each side separately. The goal becomes q, with p waiting.

00:27.646 --> 00:32.430
From hq: the first goal is exactly what hq says, so q is done.

00:32.830 --> 00:36.774
From hp: the remaining goal is p, and hp closes it.

00:37.174 --> 00:42.584
Every link can be followed, so nobody has to trust anyone. Checked by the Osprey kernel.
